  [Music]  while white travelers let these porters  shine their shoes  make their beds and serve them food the  brotherhood quietly and methodically  organized using the motto fight or be  slaves  randolph led an expansion of the union  to over eighteen  thousand members nationwide and  ironically a key to the brotherhood's  success  was the very system that relegated them  to their servile cast  the railroad the very nature of the work  enabled them to develop strong  connections among themselves  a pride and a militancy that one them  considerable  approval in the black community as a  whole porter gets on a train in new york  and he travels to atlanta and maybe down  to florida  or louisiana up to chicago or to  california  and in the process they're making  connections among communities that  otherwise might be isolated  black newspapers like the chicago  defender would use  porters to distribute their papers they  become the instruments of communication  nationwide people would get information  about what was going on in chicago  in mississippi and vice versa and the  porters were instrumental in  creating that sense of community and of  connection  this was their social network the  powerful potential of which  randolph cultivated to push for better  working conditions  and higher pay but up to this point  randolph had not yet been able to  leverage this power  beyond union organizing and collective  bargaining but that would all change  after pearl harbor  december 7th 1941  a date which will live in  infamy  as fdr's war mobilization began to lift  the nation out of the great depression  african americans were left out of the  boom black americans were  excluded by large from fairly lucrative  jobs in many cases in these defense  industries  and randolph as a union leader  raised a protest to the government that  if they did not deal with this problem  that is the racial discrimination  against black workers  that he would bring a march on  washington  and a